# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Local environment configuration (may name the real work tenant)
config.json

# Real / not-fully-de-identified data — never commit.
# See project history: SFDC file was locked to 700 rather than run through the
# re-identity rewrite (the app+users were removed from scope instead), and
# .originals/ is the explicit pre-de-identification backup with known leaked names.
App User Lists/FAKE USERS - SFDC 3rd party user list.xlsx
App User Lists/.originals/

# CONTROL EVIDENCE — TRACKED ON PURPOSE (changed 2026-07-26).
# These were previously ignored as "regenerable from the scripts + source rosters". That is
# not true: a cycle's output also depends on live tenant state at run time AND on the prior
# cycle's state.json, which carries every finding's age, ticket number and first-seen cycle.
# Losing this directory means every open finding re-tickets and no closure can be evidenced.
# state.json / SHA256SUMS / evidence_manifest.json / tickets.jsonl are the control's ledger.
#
# The workbooks and digests ARE regenerable from the ledger, so they stay out of git to keep
# the repo small — but the ledger itself is version-controlled.
cycles/**/report.xlsx
cycles/**/digest_*.md
cycles_feed/**/report.xlsx
cycles_feed/**/digest_*.md
reports/
test_rosters/

# Local run logs. The CHANGE log (logs/*.changes.jsonl) is the record of every mutating API
# call; keep it out of git (it embeds request/response bodies incl. PII) but do NOT delete
# it — archive it with the cycle evidence per your retention policy.
logs/

# Operational logs / screenshots, not project content.
*.log
pdi_keepalive_failure.png
